# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   ~ intro     room entry — The Cat & The Weaver (in the rain)
#   ~ cat       talk to Patch (grants Wall-jump)
#   ~ complete  on reaching the top — The Weaver, closing
# =============================================================================


# --- OPENING CUTSCENE: The Cat & The Weaver --------------------------------
~ intro
The cat shelters under a leaf from the rain, soaked, discouraged. The Weaver's eyes appear in the dark above, upside-down.
Weaver: You're wet, and you're doubting. Good. Doubt means you understand what's being asked. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_02_17.wav]
Cat: I can't reach it. Whatever it is. It's too high. There's a wall.
Weaver: There is ALWAYS a wall. I have spent my whole long life among walls. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_02_18.wav]
Weaver: Here is the secret no spider tells: a wall is only a barrier if you push AGAINST it. Push OFF it, and it throws you higher than open air ever could. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_02_19.wav]
Weaver: The girl you love is a wall, too, ember. Skittish thing — you keep hurling yourself at her and bouncing off and calling it failure. It isn't. It's the climb. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_02_20.wav]
Cat: ...How do you know about her.
Weaver: I told you. We watch the window. She carries my children outside on a leaf, you know. When the others would crush them. She has never once been afraid of the right things. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_02_21.wav]
Weaver: Now climb. The one who taught me about walls is here. He learned it the hard way, as the best ones do. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_02_22.wav]
=> END


# --- ABILITY CAT: Patch (grants WALL-JUMP) ---------------------------------
~ cat
A battered alley cat sits on a high ledge, watching the rain through his one good eye. He doesn't turn around.
Patch: You're the one the spider's running errands for. Heard about you. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/patch/vox_patch_room_02_23.wav]
Cat: Everyone's heard about me but me, apparently.
Patch: Funny. Most cats your size don't have a sense of humor. Too busy being scared. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/patch/vox_patch_room_02_24.wav]
Patch: You want to get up there? You gotta stop seeing walls as the end of the road. I got every one of these scars falling OFF things. Then one day I figured out the wall was the only friend I had — push off it, you go up. Hit it, kick away, hit the next one. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/patch/vox_patch_room_02_25.wav]
Patch: You don't have to make it all the way in one go. You just can't stop bouncing. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/patch/vox_patch_room_02_26.wav]
Cat: And if I fall?
Patch: Then you fall, and you climb again, and nobody up there's keeping score but you. Quit keeping score. Climb. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/patch/vox_patch_room_02_27.wav]
=> END


# --- CLOSING BEAT: The Weaver, at the top ----------------------------------
~ complete
Reaching the chandelier, the cat is exhausted but high above the rain now, the storm below him.
Weaver: You see? From down there it was a prison of glass. From up here it is a lantern in the dark. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_02_28.wav]
Weaver: Nothing changed but how high you were willing to climb. One room left, ember. Come and learn what you've been carrying toward. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_02_29.wav]
=> END
